1. **A scanning probe microscopy system for mapping a high-aspect-ratio nanostructure, the system comprising:**  
a sample stage configured to support a sample including the high-aspect-ratio nanostructure;  
a sensor head comprising a probe body, a probe tip extending from the probe body along a tip axis oriented at a nonzero oblique angle relative to a surface normal of the sample, and a sensor configured to generate a signal responsive to interaction between the probe tip and the sample;  
a positioning assembly configured to produce relative scanning motion between the sensor head and the sample in at least three spatial dimensions, such that the probe tip accesses a sidewall of the high-aspect-ratio nanostructure;  
a detachable kinematic mount coupling the sensor head to the positioning assembly, the detachable kinematic mount comprising a plurality of complementary constraint features that engage at discrete contact locations to repeatably establish a position and an angular orientation of the sensor head upon detachment and reattachment of the sensor head; and  
a controller operatively coupled to the sensor and the positioning assembly and configured to control the relative scanning motion, receive the signal from the sensor while the probe tip traverses at least an upper surface and the sidewall of the high-aspect-ratio nanostructure, and generate, from the signal and position data associated with the relative scanning motion, a three-dimensional map of the high-aspect-ratio nanostructure.

1. **A scanning probe microscope comprising:**

a sample support configured to support a sample having a surface that includes a face with a slope angle exceeding a threshold slope angle relative to a reference plane;

a carrier;

a sensor head detachably mounted to the carrier, the sensor head including a probe having a probe tip oriented at an oblique angle relative to the reference plane such that the probe tip is configured to interact with the face;

a scanning mechanism configured to produce relative scanning movement between the probe tip and the sample;

a sensor configured to generate a signal responsive to interaction between the probe tip and the face; and

cooperating mounting structures disposed respectively on the sensor head and the carrier, the cooperating mounting structures detachably coupling the sensor head to the carrier through at least three spatially separated contact points that establish a repeatable position and orientation of the sensor head relative to the carrier.
